  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preparation Sustainable Development Goals Partnership - light</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A report commissioned by the Embassy in Niamey last year has identified the agricultural value chains in which there are most opportunities to create employment for youth and women and in which the private sector is interested to invest. The most viable option that was identified was the value chain of tiger nuts (souchets). A project has since then been developed and is currently being implemented. The second value chain that came up was groundnut (arachide). This project consists of the follow-up of the study; based on the findings and identified stakeholders, a consortium will be formed that is willing to implement a project that will lead to the development of the private sector in the groundnut value chain, that will create jobs especially for youth and women and that will contribute to the goals set by the Embassy regarding sustainable development.</narrative>
  </description>
